<Site title="Privacy" description="How address search handles your information."><div class="page-top"><h1>Privacy</h1></div><section class="card"><h2>Place and address search</h2><p>Using place or address suggestions anywhere on the site sends your search text and browser information to Google Maps Platform. Google’s <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> applies to that service.</p><p>When you select a province, town or other area, Counted receives its selected name, area type, province and representative coordinates to match our results directory. This request is not cached or saved to our datasets.</p><p>When you select an address or landmark, your browser sends its coordinates to Counted to find the electoral ward. Our lookup does not save your address, selected place or coordinates. They are not added to our public datasets. The selected place stays in this page until you leave or choose another location. The Explore map page saves its visible map position and selected electoral area in the page URL, so copying that link shares the map view. It does not include your address text or Google place ID.</p><h2>Site requests</h2><p>Our hosting provider processes network requests to deliver the site and protect it from abuse. Avoid entering sensitive information in public search URLs. Election results and geographic boundaries are public data.</p></section></Site>
